KNOWNBUG libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp20 --stdlib libc++
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ invoke_result_t: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
libc++ (LLVM 18): std::invoke_result_t of a std::__bind_back closure
(N5008 [meta.trans.other], [func.require]) -- "symbol 'R' is unknown",
although calling the closure works (cpp20_libcxx_header_drops/bind_back.cpp).
The smallest known part of cpp20_ranges_basic_libcxx.  A cvise reduction
drifted to cpp11_inheriting_constructors_keep_implicit_default_constructor
(the reduced __perfect_forward_impl lost its constructors), so this one is
not reduced yet.  clang++ 18 -stdlib=libc++ accepts this program, and it
fails only its WRONG assertion.
